@flexiarg operator/sibling-agents-compare-notes
@title Sibling Agents Compare Notes — 'Do a Short Whistle Exchange to Find Common Ground'
@status accepted 2026-11-11: proposed by 象 for 2 turns (Joe 2026-11-11: recurrence suffices); attested once used in a mission or a War Machine cascade
@provenance 象 proposals, ~/.emacs-graph/session-turn-analysis/<record>[.json].candidates.json; records: turn-0AANsl turn-IH3Rmr; first proposed for: Two agents hold adjacent pieces of one problem (claude-6 on priority ordering, codex-7 on Inbox-Zero/warrant freshness).
@why [collaboration-coherence/isolation]

! conclusion: Direct one agent to a short, bounded exchange with the other ('a short whistle exchange… to find common ground'), and name the shared frame to test (here: the library/hygiene patterns apply in all cases).

  + IF:
    The adjacency has been named and the cheapest next step is direct peer contact rather than operator-mediated synthesis.

  + HOWEVER:
    The operator synthesising both sides himself becomes the bottleneck and loses the agents' local detail; leaving them uncoupled repeats the isolation.

  + THEN:
    Direct one agent to a short, bounded exchange with the other ('a short whistle exchange… to find common ground'), and name the shared frame to test (here: the library/hygiene patterns apply in all cases).

  + BECAUSE:
    The parent says schedule and structure the coupling; this is the coupling act delegated to the agents themselves, bounded in cost ('short') and given a hypothesis to test ('common ground').
